     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Only mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin are deployed, so all other defence constants (patched_*, segmented, mfa_user) are false. The attacker can still get deep into the network: exploit_web gives foothold_web, pivot_internal gives reach_internal (not segmented), steal_user_cred gives stolen_user, auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver (mfa_user is false), and kerberoast gives stolen_admin. escalate_ciserver and leak_secrets_ciserver can even give stolen_dbadmin. However, auth_dc and auth_adfs require NOT mfa_admin, so foothold_dc and foothold_adfs, and therefore admin_dc and admin_adfs, are unreachable. auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs), which is false. So no foothold on db, fileserver or backup is possible. That means no admin on them, and no exfiltrate technique can fire. exfiltrated is unreachable.\"}"
    }
   ],
